# Back-flow PRs — ACTIVE BY DEFAULT (AR-25).
# Shipping this commented out meant a back-flow PR fell through to
# `* @placeholder-admin` — one approver — so the two-reviewer confidentiality
# rule had no routing at all out of the box, and branch protection cannot fix
# a commented-out line.
#
# Pattern B adopters (no external client work, so no back-flow): DELETE the two
# lines below. Leaving them costs one extra reviewer on those folders; deleting
# them by mistake under Pattern A silently removes a confidentiality gate. The
# safe default is on.
#
# Note what this does NOT cover: AR-27 (the 500-line cap is measured per PR, so
# four 400-line PRs clear it) and AR-28 (nothing verifies that two *distinct*
# humans approved). Routing alone is not the whole control.
/domain-*/methods/             @placeholder-admin
/domain-*/prompts/             @placeholder-admin
